{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-practical-roleplay-daily-talk-in-new-york-city-subway-london-cafe-madrid-plaza-berlin-k/audio/main-87c0db23d47f.mp3","durationSec":150.96,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.9,"text":"Imagine a short conversation on a New York City subway train."},{"start":4.62,"end":8.2,"text":"You are standing near another passenger, and your bag is between you."},{"start":8.78,"end":10.96,"text":"You want to move without touching the other person."},{"start":11.46,"end":14.04,"text":"A simple opening is enough: ‘Excuse me.’"},{"start":14.78,"end":18.08,"text":"Then explain your request: ‘Could you move your bag a little, please?’"},{"start":18.92,"end":22.46,"text":"The passenger can answer, ‘Of course,’ and move it beside their feet."},{"start":23.26,"end":26.06,"text":"You can then stand in the space and say, ‘Thank you.’"},{"start":26.62,"end":29.64,"text":"If someone asks you to move, answer before you act."},{"start":30.28,"end":32.78,"text":"‘Sure, I can move’ tells them you understood."},{"start":33.66,"end":39.26,"text":"This exchange is about sharing space, not asking for a route or a train time."},{"start":40.66,"end":42.58,"text":"Picture a conversation in a London cafe."},{"start":43.46,"end":46.42,"text":"You see people waiting, but you do not know who is last."},{"start":47.3,"end":50.2,"text":"Ask a person near the end, ‘Are you waiting in the queue?’"},{"start":50.94,"end":54.54,"text":"If they say yes, ask, ‘Can I stand behind you?’"},{"start":55.16,"end":57.76,"text":"Their answer gives you a clear place to wait."},{"start":57.76,"end":60.52,"text":"You do not need to guess or walk in front of anyone."},{"start":61.22,"end":64.96,"text":"If you miss the answer, say, ‘Sorry, could you say that again?’"},{"start":65.86,"end":68.2,"text":"The other person can repeat it in simple words."},{"start":68.94,"end":70.84,"text":"Finish with ‘Thanks’ and join the queue."},{"start":71.74,"end":77.1,"text":"These questions concern the people beside you; they do not require information about prices or opening hours."},{"start":78.08,"end":80.56,"text":"Imagine sitting beside someone in Madrid’s Plaza Mayor."},{"start":81.16,"end":84.88,"text":"There is a bag on the next seat, so ask, ‘Is someone sitting here?’"},{"start":85.86,"end":90.62,"text":"If the person says their friend is using it, answer, ‘No problem,’ and leave the seat free."},{"start":92.06,"end":93.7,"text":"Now picture an office kitchen in Berlin."},{"start":94.64,"end":98.1,"text":"A colleague has a cup beside the sink, and you want to wash your own cup."},{"start":98.7,"end":100.98,"text":"Ask, ‘Are you still using this space?’"},{"start":101.58,"end":103.76,"text":"The colleague can finish or make room for you."},{"start":104.42,"end":108.34,"text":"In both examples, a question is better than moving another person’s things."},{"start":109.08,"end":110.9,"text":"Listen to the answer before you act."},{"start":110.9,"end":113.46,"text":"A polite answer can be yes or no."},{"start":114.04,"end":116.28,"text":"Picture a short exchange inside a Paris bakery."},{"start":116.28,"end":119.68,"text":"You are near the door when another customer wants to leave."},{"start":120.38,"end":122.52,"text":"The customer says, ‘Excuse me, could I get past?’"},{"start":123.26,"end":125.68,"text":"You can answer, ‘Of course,’ and move to the side."},{"start":126.38,"end":129.58,"text":"If you also need to leave, ask, ‘Are you going out too?’"},{"start":130.4,"end":133.36,"text":"A clear answer helps you decide who will move first."},{"start":134.22,"end":137.88,"text":"‘Yes, please go first’ makes the next action easy to understand."},{"start":138.55,"end":142.26,"text":"You can say, ‘Thanks,’ walk through the door, and finish the conversation."},{"start":143.22,"end":145.96,"text":"Nobody needs a long explanation about why they are leaving."},{"start":146.7,"end":150.52,"text":"The important thing is to make your request clear and give the other person room."}],"words":[{"text":"Imagine","start":0,"end":0.38},{"text":"a","start":0.38,"end":0.66},{"text":"short","start":0.66,"end":0.92},{"text":"conversation","start":0.92,"end":1.54},{"text":"on","start":1.54,"end":2.1},{"text":"a","start":2.1,"end":2.26},{"text":"New","start":2.26,"end":2.42},{"text":"York","start":2.42,"end":2.66},{"text":"City","start":2.66,"end":3.02},{"text":"subway","start":3.02,"end":3.4},{"text":"train","start":3.4,"end":3.9},{"text":"You","start":4.62,"end":4.7},{"text":"are","start":4.7,"end":4.84},{"text":"standing","start":4.84,"end":5.18},{"text":"near","start":5.18,"end":5.48},{"text":"another","start":5.48,"end":5.82},{"text":"passenger","start":5.82,"end":6.32},{"text":"and","start":6.7,"end":6.98},{"text":"your","start":6.98,"end":7.12},{"text":"bag","start":7.12,"end":7.4},{"text":"is","start":7.4,"end":7.56},{"text":"between","start":7.56,"end":7.94},{"text":"you","start":7.94,"end":8.2},{"text":"You","start":8.78,"end":9},{"text":"want","start":9,"end":9.18},{"text":"to","start":9.18,"end":9.4},{"text":"move","start":9.4,"end":9.58},{"text":"without","start":9.58,"end":9.88},{"text":"touching","start":9.88,"end":10.24},{"text":"the","start":10.24,"end":10.4},{"text":"other","start":10.4,"end":10.56},{"text":"person","start":10.56,"end":10.96},{"text":"A","start":11.46,"end":11.68},{"text":"simple","start":11.68,"end":11.98},{"text":"opening","start":11.98,"end":12.38},{"text":"is","start":12.38,"end":12.58},{"text":"enough","start":12.58,"end":12.86},{"text":"Excuse","start":13.3,"end":13.66},{"text":"me","start":13.66,"end":14.04},{"text":"Then","start":14.78,"end":15.06},{"text":"explain","start":15.06,"end":15.44},{"text":"your","start":15.44,"end":15.64},{"text":"request","start":15.64,"end":16.04},{"text":"Could","start":16.62,"end":16.72},{"text":"you","start":16.72,"end":16.88},{"text":"move","start":16.88,"end":17.06},{"text":"your","start":17.06,"end":17.24},{"text":"bag","start":17.2